    version.set("251.23774.466")  // << too new, unpublished yet
    type.set("PS")
}
 251 is PhpStorm 2025.1 Early Access or something crazy new 
but JetBrains hasn't published artifacts for PhpStorm 2025 yet!

Result: Gradle cannot find it  fails to build.

 TL;DR:
You cannot directly target arbitrary PhpStorm versions (unless JetBrains uploaded artifacts).

You can only target released, available builds.

 Here's the right solution:
Option 1:
Use IntelliJ IDEA Community artifacts (even though you develop for PhpStorm).

Because HTML parsing, PsiReference, XmlTag, etc.
are all part of com.intellij.modules.platform, not PhpStorm-specific.

kotlin
Copy
Edit
