    version.set("241.14494.240")   // <-- example: 2024.1 release
    type.set("IC")                  // <-- IntelliJ Community
}
 This will always work.

You still develop for PhpStorm, it doesnt matter 
what matters is you use the correct SDK.

In short:
PhpStorm is a custom skin over IntelliJ + plugins.
For 99% of plugin cases, just use IC.

Option 2 (advanced):
If you really want to target PhpStorm,
you have to:

Download PhpStorm SDK manually,

Point Gradle to it explicitly,

Deal with version mismatches manually.

