 Step 1: Highlight unresolved tags in RED
 How IntelliJ does it:
We must create a LocalInspectionTool that:

Checks if the resolve() inside our TaglibFileReference returns null.

If yes  mark the tag as an error.

 Create new file:
src/main/java/com/lucianpopescu/viewlanguage/TaglibMissingInspection.java

java
Copy
Edit
package com.lucianpopescu.viewlanguage;

import com.intellij.codeInspection.LocalInspectionTool;
import com.intellij.codeInspection.ProblemsHolder;
import com.intellij.codeInspection.ProblemHighlightType;
import com.intellij.psi.PsiElementVisitor;
import com.intellij.psi.xml.XmlTag;
import org.jetbrains.annotations.NotNull;

public class TaglibMissingInspection extends LocalInspectionTool {

    @Override
    public @NotNull PsiElementVisitor buildVisitor(@NotNull ProblemsHolder holder, boolean isOnTheFly) {
        return new XmlTagVisitor(holder);
    }

    private static class XmlTagVisitor extends com.intellij.psi.XmlElementVisitor {
        private final ProblemsHolder holder;

        XmlTagVisitor(ProblemsHolder holder) {
            this.holder = holder;
        }

        @Override
        public void visitXmlTag(@NotNull XmlTag tag) {
            String fullName = tag.getName(); // like popup:add

            if (!fullName.contains(":")) {
                return; // not a taglib tag
            }

            String[] parts = fullName.split(":");
            if (parts.length != 2) {
                return;
            }

            String library = parts[0];
            String name = parts[1];

            String expectedPath = "application/taglib/" + library + "/" + name + ".html";

            var file = tag.getProject().getBaseDir().findFileByRelativePath(expectedPath);

            if (file == null) {
                holder.registerProblem(
                    tag,
                    "Cannot resolve taglib file: " + expectedPath,
                    ProblemHighlightType.ERROR
                );
            }
        }
    }
}
 This will underline in RED if the taglib file is missing.

 Step 2: Register the inspection inside plugin.xml
Inside your src/main/resources/META-INF/plugin.xml, add:

